WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.279
Hi and welcome.

1
00:00:02.619 --> 00:00:06.449
If you've ever walked into an art meeting feeling unprepared,

2
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.559
you're not alone.

3
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.630
An AR meeting is where the team plans

4
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.630
a student's special education services for the year.

5
00:00:14.069 --> 00:00:14.670
Families,

6
00:00:14.829 --> 00:00:15.390
teachers,

7
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.379
administrators,

8
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.520
and evaluators all bring something to the table.

9
00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:21.069
When teachers come ready,

10
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.649
the meeting runs smoother,

11
00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:24.069
families feel heard,

12
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.670
and the plan actually fits the student.

13
00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:28.979
In the next 10 minutes,

14
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.719
you'll learn 3 things.

15
00:00:31.139 --> 00:00:31.680
First,

16
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.900
what to gather 2 to 3 weeks before the meeting.

17
00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:35.919
Second,

18
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.680
how to share data with families in plain,

19
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.180
specific language.

20
00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:41.189
And third,

21
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.380
what to do after the meeting so the new plan works in your classroom.

22
00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:47.029
At the end,

23
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:51.409
you can download a one-page checklist to keep for every ARD meeting.

24
00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:52.610
Let's get started.